description:
Godrej \& Boyce Mfg. Co. Ltd. ( G\&B ), a part of the Godrej Enterprises Group, has played a key role in India’s economic history by driving excellence in design and manufacturing and delivering sustainable value for its stakeholders and communities.




 Godrej Enterprises Group's diverse presence across 10 industries \- from complex engineering solutions to consumer goods like storage solutions, furniture and security solutions \- positively impacts the lives of one\-third of India's population every day.




 Through international subsidiaries and joint ventures, the company's products have also established a strong global footprint across 5 continents.




 As a value\-driven company known for its integrity and strong social conscience, it has built a compassionate corporate culture designed to empower the individuals, teams and communities that the Godrej Enterprises operates in. For this, Godrej Enterprises has been consistently recognized as one of India's most respected companies. Our focus on customers for over a century has helped us constantly innovate; design products and solutions with clarity of purpose that are manufactured in a quality\-driven and technology\- led environment and distributed through a national and international network of partners. Strong sustainable practices that help protect the environment are also enshrined in our Good \& Green policy that remains at the core of Godrej Enterprise Group’s business operations.










**Job Profile:\-**










**Key Responsibility Areas\-** 



* Conducting legal due diligence and advising the business team on the title in respect of properties Pan India;
* Advising business teams on real estate transactions, including residential and commercial properties;
* Drafting Real Estate transaction documents, either to sell/ purchase the property or lease/ license of the properties; and
* Preparing Dashboard summary of the transaction status update and the way forward.









**Job** 
**Description\-** 



* Conducting legal due diligence for verifying the title of seller or lessor or licensor of the property before commencement of the transaction;
* Providing legal opinion to the Business team in respect of the property ownership, encumbrances and compliance with respect to the applicable laws;
* Coordinating with concerned persons of verticals from the various divisions and other stakeholders PAN India for smooth completion of the transactions;
* Drafting, reviewing and finalizing real estate transaction documents such as term sheet/ letter of intent, leave \& license agreements, lease deeds, extension letters, letter of attornment, agreement for sale, sale deeds, etc.;
* Advising the business team on the stamp duty payable on the transaction documents;
* Advising the business team on compliance with the applicable real estate laws, statutes, government regulations and contractual obligations under the transaction documents;
* Periodically preparing and updating the Dashboard summary of the transactions, Status update and the way forward;
* Conduct legal workshops and make presentations to the business teams to provide guidance and training on real estate laws and legal compliance.









**Requisite Qualification\-** 




**Essential\-** 
 Graduate in any discipline with LLB.




**Preferred\-** 
 Mumbai.










**Requisite Experience\-** 




**Essential\-** 
 Advocate having at least 5 years of Real Estate experience.




**Preferred\-** 
 Land Related Litigation.










**Special Skills Required:\-** 




**Essential:** 




 1\. Computer Savvy;




 2\. Knowledge on Land Laws;




 3\. Well conversed with reading of Marathi documents;




 4\. Hands on experience in Real Estate transactions;




 5\. Researching abilities regarding legal issues;




 6\. Excellent drafting skills.
